course: dictionary
lesson: 9578
title: Clouds that lie flat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists give clouds names so we can talk about them. Some clouds are puffy, some are wispy, and some are flat. Stratus is the word for the flat ones. Its name comes from Latin and means "spread out", which tells you what it looks like.
explain: «Stratus clouds are low flat grey sheets.» Look at the clues: low means close to the ground, flat means no bumps, and grey means a dull colour. A stratus cloud spreads over the sky like a blanket.
explain: Stratus clouds often bring drizzle or mist, which are light rain and damp air. When stratus sits right on the ground, we call it fog. To check your meaning, swap it into a sentence: "The grey stratus covered the sky like a blanket" still makes sense.
fact: Stratus is a type of low, flat, grey cloud.
fact: Stratus covers the sky like a blanket.
fact: Stratus often brings drizzle or mist.
fact: Stratus at ground level is fog.
fact: Stratus means "spread out" in Latin, which is why it describes flat layers.
exercise: «Stratus clouds are low flat grey sheets.» What kind of cloud is stratus? | A dark storm cloud with thunder | *A low, flat, grey cloud | A thin wisp of ice high up | A tall, puffy white cloud
exercise: Stratus at ground level is called what? | Sunshine | Hail | Rainbow | *Fog
exercise: Which word fits? "The flat grey ___ covered the whole sky like a blanket." | cirrus | cumulus | *stratus | cumulonimbus
test: What does the Latin root of stratus mean? | *Spread out | Very dark | Very high | Puffy like a heap
test: «Stratus clouds often bring» which weather? | Hot sunshine and no clouds | Hailstones the size of eggs | Snowstorms with thunder | *Drizzle or mist
exam: Mia says stratus is a puffy white cloud on sunny days. Is she right? | No, stratus is a kind of rain shower | *No, that is cumulus; stratus is flat and grey | Yes, stratus is puffy and white | Yes, stratus only forms at night
